#: ../../../generators.rst:3
msgid "C Runtime, Compiler and Build System Generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:8
msgid "Build system generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:10
msgid ""
"Since scikit-build simply provides glue between ``setuptools`` and "
"``CMake``, a `CMake generator`_ is used to configure the build system "
"allowing to build of CPython C extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:18
msgid ""
"scikit-build no longer probes for installed Visual Studio versions or runs a "
"language test to discover a working generator. CMake's own default generator "
"selection applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:22
msgid ""
"CMake selects its default generator for the current platform, and the "
"``CMAKE_GENERATOR`` environment variable can be used to override it::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:25
msgid "CMAKE_GENERATOR=\"Unix Makefiles\" pip install ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:27
msgid ""
"``Ninja`` is the recommended generator. It is automatically parallel and is "
"available on all platforms. The recommended ``scikit_build_core.setuptools."
"build_meta`` backend (see :ref:`basic_usage_example`) adds the `ninja python "
"package <https://pypi.org/project/ninja/>`_ to the build requirements "
"automatically when no suitable build tool is already available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:34
msgid ""
"For more details about CMake generators, see the `CMake documentation "
"<https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/manual/cmake-generators.7.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generators.rst:40
msgid "Compiler"
